          "title": "You'll want to know: લાકડું",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "લાકડું — lākḍũ — \"wood\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "આ ખુરશી જૂના લાકડાની છે. ā khurśī jūnā lākḍānī che. This chair is made of old wood."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A neuter noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "લાકડું (lākḍũ) goes back to Sanskrit lakuṭa, \"a club, a stick\", and CDIAL lists the Gujarati word with the sense \"stick\" (CDIAL 10875). In everyday Gujarati it names wood itself, the stuff a chair or a door is made of."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
