          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "આવડવું — āvaḍvũ — \"to know how (to do something)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "મીરાને લાકડાનું કામ આવડે છે. Mīrāne lākḍānũ kām āvḍe che. Mira knows how to do woodwork."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (it …): તે કામ તેને આવડી ગયું, te kām tene āvḍī gayũ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "આવડવું (āvaḍvũ) takes the person who has the skill with ને, and the skill itself is the subject: મને તરતાં આવડે છે, I know how to swim. CDIAL lists the Gujarati verb, \"to come to someone's knowledge\", under Sanskrit āpatati, \"flies towards; befalls\" (CDIAL 1193); the step to knowing a skill is not explained there."
            }
          ]
        },
